  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Why Does My Handrail Feel Loose?",
    "text": "Why Does My Handrail Feel Loose?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "It's pretty unsettling when your handrail starts to feel wobbly, isn't it? Often, the first thing people wonder is if it's truly unsafe or just a minor issue. Usually, looseness comes down to a few key areas: the brackets, newel posts, or balusters. Sometimes, it's a simple case of worn fasteners or anchors. We see this all the time across Denver and surrounding areas, from Aurora to Colorado Springs. It’s important not to just ignore it, as even a little wiggle can become a safety hazard. Before you panic, a quick check can often reveal if it's a surface-level problem or something more structural. Knowing the difference helps you decide if a simple fix will do or if you need to call in a pro to make sure it's truly secure again.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
